{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.BringWPlaneMonodromy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BringWPlaneMonodromy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Determinant.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.monodromy_satisfies_recurrence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.monodromy_satisfies_recurrence","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BringWPlaneMonodromy.lean#L85-L94","doc":"**The carried monodromy satisfies the recurrence kernel (sorry-free, from the class).**\nAny `BringWPlaneMonodromy` instance's operator obeys `M² = (tr M)·M − I` — the depth-2 recurrence\nkernel `R(x) = x² − (tr M)·x + 1`, with `τ = tr M`. Discharged from `unimodular_two_recurrence`\napplied to the class's `unimodular` field; the geometric identification (`is_seifert_gauss_manin`)\nis not needed for the *algebraic* recurrence — only for the open claim that this `M` is the genuine\nSeifert monodromy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BringWPlaneMonodromy.seifert_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BringWPlaneMonodromy.seifert_holds","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BringWPlaneMonodromy.lean#L83-L83","doc":"**The conjecture**: the geometric identification holds — `M` is the genuine Seifert /\nGauss–Manin monodromy of `E = Bring/S₄` along the S³/2I fibration (the §3b conjectural input).\n\n**Parameterised 2026-09-13.**  `is_seifert_gauss_manin` was a *field* typed with the\nuniverse `Prop` alongside this witness, so the instance chose the proposition and\n`⟨True, trivial⟩` discharged the pair — the geometric identification, which the class\ndocstring calls the conjecture's whole *content*, cost nothing to assume.  As a parameter\nit is fixed by the binder and visible in every consumer's type.\n\nIt is a parameter rather than an encoding deliberately: identifying `M` with the genuine\nSeifert monodromy is the open geometric claim itself, so writing a proposition for it here\nwould be guessing at the conjecture rather than carrying it.  `monodromy_satisfies_recurrence`\nbelow is unaffected — it uses `unimodular` only, and never this field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BringWPlaneMonodromy.unimodular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BringWPlaneMonodromy.unimodular","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BringWPlaneMonodromy.lean#L69-L69","doc":"Unimodular: `det M = 1` (the symplectic structure of `H¹` of an elliptic curve). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BringWPlaneMonodromy.M","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BringWPlaneMonodromy.M","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BringWPlaneMonodromy.lean#L67-L67","doc":"The Gauss–Manin monodromy operator on the rank-2 W-plane `H¹(E)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BringWPlaneMonodromy.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BringWPlaneMonodromy.mk","kind":"ctor","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BringWPlaneMonodromy.lean#L65-L65","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.BringWPlaneMonodromy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.BringWPlaneMonodromy","kind":"class","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BringWPlaneMonodromy.lean#L56-L83","doc":"**Bring W-plane Gauss–Manin monodromy** — §3b conjecture class (numerology-guarded).\n\nThe conjecture: there is a unimodular `2×2` operator `M` that is the *actual* Gauss–Manin /\nSeifert monodromy of the W-plane elliptic fibre `E = Bring/S₄` along the S³/2I fibration, whose\ntrace is the depth-2 recurrence kernel coefficient `τ` (#2488). By `unimodular_two_recurrence`, such\nan `M` automatically satisfies the recurrence kernel `x² − τ·x + 1` (Cayley–Hamilton) — so the\nconjecture's *content* is the **geometric identification** of `M`, not the kernel's form (which is\nforced) nor the value of `τ` (which is never fitted). The falsifiable functional target is that the\n*same* `M` reproduces the whole `(n−1,1)` recurrence family, not the single scalar `τ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.unimodular_two_recurrence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.unimodular_two_recurrence","kind":"theorem","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/BringWPlaneMonodromy.lean#L36-L54","doc":"**The recurrence kernel is the Cayley–Hamilton relation of a unimodular 2×2 monodromy.**\nFor any `M ∈ Mat₂(ℝ)` with `det M = 1` (a symplectic / `SL₂` monodromy on the rank-2 W-plane\n`H¹(E)`, `E = Bring/S₄`), `M·M = (tr M)·M − I` — i.e. `M` satisfies the depth-2 recurrence kernel\n`R(x) = x² − τ·x + 1` with `τ = tr M`. The monic, unit-constant-term form of the kernel (#2488) is\nthus **forced** by unimodularity; this is the operator-level (functional) content, **not** the trace\nvalue `τ ≈ 2.6424` (which the numerology guardrail forbids fitting). ","signatureChunk":0}]}